  1581	
  1582	        ``enforce_floor`` (the tick-signing floor, decision design/tick-signing
  1583	        -era-is-a-floor) is ON BY DEFAULT: when no signature was produced AND
  1584	        the store is already in the signed era, refuse — raise
  1585	        ``UnsignedTickInSignedEra`` BEFORE writing, so no unsigned tick is
  1586	        appended and the chain's era-monotonicity holds. Default-on makes the
  1587	        invariant fail-safe: every live mint (each verb that fires a boundary —
  1588	        ``sl seal``, ``sl emit <v> seal``, count/predicate boundaries — and any
  1589	        other live caller such as the tasks harness) is protected without
  1590	        opting in. Only re-mint paths that reconstruct history under their own
  1591	        signer wiring (rebirth/slice/replay) pass ``enforce_floor=False`` — the
  1592	        exemptions are named, not the enforcement.
  1593	
  1594	        Chain semantics (see design/tick-chain-at-store-layer):
  1595	        - prev_hash: sha256 of the previous tick row (any era) — None for
  1596	          the first row in the store.
  1597	        - window bounds are explicit fact ids; membership and ordering are
  1598	          APPEND ORDER (rowid), never id order — the cursor is the id of the
  1599	          newest fact BY ROWID, not MAX(id) (see ORDERING AUTHORITY above):
  1600	          - first tick in a new store: window_start "" (covers all facts);
  1601	          - first chained tick after pre-chain rows: window_start =
  1602	            current append edge (epoch marker — claims no coverage of
  1603	            history it cannot vouch for);
  1604	          - otherwise: window_start = previous tick's fact_cursor.
  1605	        - window_hash commits to every fact row in (window_start, fact_cursor].
  1606	        - signature (delta 2): when a tick_signer was injected, signs the
  1607	          commitment hash of the new row; NULL otherwise (pre-signature era).
  1608	        """
  1609	        return self.append_tick_attested(tick, enforce_floor=enforce_floor)[0]
