   180	def object_of_batch(rows: list[tuple]) -> dict:
   181	    """A multi-row ceremony as ONE atomic record object.
   182	
   183	    ``rows`` are fact row tuples in emission order. One row collapses to a
   184	    plain fact object — a 1-row batch would be a second spelling of the same
   185	    record (the "signature must be absent, not null" ethos), so the envelope
   186	    exists only where multi-row atomicity does. Zero rows is a caller bug.
