codex
Reviewed r2 at `b5628350`, read-only. The redesign materially improves r1, but D0 still lacks a realizable invariant/migration design, and D4’s registry extraction is underspecified in a way that conflicts with its exact-admission-set promise.

## DP-r1 re-verification

| Finding | Verdict | Evidence |
|---|---|---|
| DP-r1-01 | PASS | The rewound-marker capability now survives as an indexed query for coordinates beyond the consumed ordinal ([design-proposal.md:70](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/docs/scratch/arrival-sliceD/design-proposal.md:70), [design-proposal.md:320](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/docs/scratch/arrival-sliceD/design-proposal.md:320)). The proposal also correctly limits anchor validation to self-consistency; source confirms it does not establish chaining to genesis ([arrival.py:1149](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/libs/engine/src/engine/arrival.py:1149)). |
| DP-r1-02 | PASS | Arrival-canonical migration is now log-derived, preserving shared batch ordinals, with rederivation on mismatch ([design-proposal.md:135](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/docs/scratch/arrival-sliceD/design-proposal.md:135)). This matches the source expansion model: one record can yield multiple rows ([arrival_projection.py:153](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/libs/engine/src/engine/arrival_projection.py:153), [arrival_store.py:342](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/libs/engine/src/engine/arrival_store.py:342)). |
| DP-r1-03 | FAIL | The proposed enforcement remains internally incomplete. A unique index permits multiple NULL coordinates in SQLite; merely adding columns to a shared INSERT does not reject explicitly supplied NULLs. The promised “CHECK-equivalent enforcement at the single insert statement” is neither defined nor schema-enforced ([design-proposal.md:115](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/docs/scratch/arrival-sliceD/design-proposal.md:115), [design-proposal.md:119](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/docs/scratch/arrival-sliceD/design-proposal.md:119)). Existing shared insert SQL accepts whatever tuple its callers supply ([sqlite_store.py:746](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/libs/engine/src/engine/sqlite_store.py:746), [arrival_store.py:351](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/libs/engine/src/engine/arrival_store.py:351)). See DP-r2-01/02. |
| DP-r1-04 | PASS | Both construction and verification paths are now enumerated, including the two rowid-based verification counts visible in source ([design-proposal.md:261](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/docs/scratch/arrival-sliceD/design-proposal.md:261), [sqlite_store.py:1902](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/libs/engine/src/engine/sqlite_store.py:1902), [sqlite_store.py:1929](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/libs/engine/src/engine/sqlite_store.py:1929)). The permutation gate directly covers the prior omission. |
| DP-r1-05 | PASS | `ArrivalLog.anchor(mark)` now returns the consumed anchor itself, and the proposal accurately treats the offset as an internal seek hint ([design-proposal.md:329](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/docs/scratch/arrival-sliceD/design-proposal.md:329)). Source confirms `_anchor_for` already returns the anchor while `walk_marked` yields only subsequent records ([arrival.py:1173](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/libs/engine/src/engine/arrival.py:1173), [arrival.py:1218](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/libs/engine/src/engine/arrival.py:1218)). |
| DP-r1-06 | PASS | The admission check is now correctly defined over post-dedup fact rows, their carried signatures, and `fact_commitment_hash` ([design-proposal.md:403](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/docs/scratch/arrival-sliceD/design-proposal.md:403)). Source confirms the content-only commitment excludes custody context ([sqlite_store.py:254](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/libs/engine/src/engine/sqlite_store.py:254)) and merge carries the row signature verbatim ([merge.py:512](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/libs/store/src/store/merge.py:512)). The original finding is dissolved, though registry extraction has a new hole below. |
